From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:42:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: validation on a real module; PLT split, lift limits and
 parallel build found by it (T7)

module_validate.py measures lifting coverage and runs leaf functions of a module next to Unicorn on random
inputs (also through the JIT). Run on the five modules of a retail game it found three faults, fixed here:
the PLT has one unwind entry for all its stubs, so a call into it is an entry and the function is split
(subsdk1 would not build); remill-lift takes the code as one argument, so a function over 60,000 bytes is a
LiftError run by the JIT (main would not build); find_functions was quadratic. Aot lifts and compiles many
functions in parallel. 280 real functions equal to Unicorn over 2,658 cases, no difference.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: validation tooling and fixes of the AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); no game data in the tests, which use synthetic modules
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t7-module-reel)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
